\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. All my hope on God is founded;
\par He doth still my trust renew,
\par Me through change and chance He guideth,
\par Only good and only true.
\par God unknown,
\par He alone
\par Calls my heart to be His own.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Pride of man and earthly glory,
\par Sword and crown betray his trust:
\par What with care and toil he buildeth,
\par Tower and temple fall to dust,
\par But God's power,
\par Hour by hour,
\par Is my temple and my tower.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. God's great goodness aye endureth,
\par Deep His wisdom passing thought:
\par Splendour, light, and life attend Him,
\par Beauty springeth out of nought,
\par Evermore
\par From His store
\par New-born worlds rise and adore.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Daily doth the Almighty Giver
\par Bounteous gifts on us bestow.
\par His desire our soul delighteth,
\par Pleasure leads us where we go.
\par Love doth stand
\par At  His hand;
\par Joy doth wait on His command.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Still from man to God eternal
\par Sacrifice of praise be done,
\par High above all praises praising
\par For the gift of Christ His Son.
\par Christ doth call
\par One and all:
\par Ye who follow shall not fall.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

